Job Purpose&nbsp; 

We are seeking an experienced Backend Developer to contribute to the development and maintenance of a high-performance Loan Origination System (LOS). The ideal candidate will have strong expertise in Java, Spring Boot, and building scalable enterprise applications in the financial services domain. &nbsp; 

Key Responsibilities&nbsp; 

Development and Implementation&nbsp; 

- Design, develop, and maintain RESTful APIs for the Loan Origination System. &nbsp; 
 - Implement event-driven workflows for application processing. &nbsp; 
 - Develop asynchronous processing solutions for high-throughput scenarios. &nbsp; 
 - Integrate with third-party services. &nbsp; 
 - Implement caching strategies using Redis to optimize performance. &nbsp; 
 - Build robust error-handling and retry mechanisms for external service calls. &nbsp; 

Performance and Scalability&nbsp; 

- Optimize database queries and connection pooling for PostgreSQL and MySQL. &nbsp; 
 - Manage thread pools for asynchronous operations. &nbsp; 
 - Monitor and optimize application performance under high load. &nbsp; 

Architecture and Design&nbsp; 

- Apply clean architecture principles and design patterns, including Strategy, Factory, and Builder. &nbsp; 
 - Implement microservices-style integrations with clear separation of concerns. &nbsp; 
 - Design and implement callback-handling mechanisms for asynchronous operations. &nbsp; 
 - Build reusable components and services in line with SOLID principles. &nbsp; 

Data Management&nbsp; 

- Work with PostgreSQL and MySQL using JPA/Hibernate. &nbsp; 
 - Implement efficient data-access patterns and repository layers. &nbsp; 
 - Handle data migration and synchronization between systems. &nbsp; 

Quality and Testing&nbsp; 

- Write unit and integration tests using TestNG and related testing frameworks. &nbsp; 
 - Implement comprehensive error handling and logging. &nbsp; 
 - Maintain code quality through code reviews and engineering best practices. &nbsp; 
 - Debug and resolve production issues. &nbsp; 

Required Skills and Experience&nbsp; 

- Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, or a related field. &nbsp; 
 - At least 4 years of relevant software development experience. &nbsp; 
 - Strong proficiency in Java 17+, including object-oriented programming, collections, concurrency, and multithreading. &nbsp; 
 - Experience with Spring Boot 3. x, Spring Security (OAuth2), Spring Data JPA, WebFlux, and AOP. &nbsp; 
 - Strong knowledge of PostgreSQL, MySQL, JPA/Hibernate, HikariCP, and query optimization. &nbsp; 
 - Experience with Redis and distributed caching strategies. &nbsp; 
 - Familiarity with Maven build tools. &nbsp; 
 - Experience with testing frameworks and libraries such as TestNG, JUnit, and Mockito. &nbsp; 

Good to Have&nbsp; 

- Experience with MongoDB. &nbsp; 
 - Experience with Apache Kafka for event-driven architecture and high-throughput messaging. &nbsp;

Years of Experience: &nbsp; 5 - 8 Years&nbsp; 

