About the Role&nbsp; 

DoctusTech builds AI agents for value-based care organizations, covering HCC risk adjustment, &nbsp; coding compliance, HEDIS, and clinical documentation. &nbsp; 

This is a hands-on role. You will personally review AI outputs against medical records, quantify&nbsp; accuracy, build the models that measure clinical and financial impact, and give engineering&nbsp; precise, evidence-backed feedback. You will be the clinical quality gate before anything ships to&nbsp; customers. &nbsp; 

Key Responsibilities&nbsp; 

Clinical QA of AI Outputs&nbsp; 

• Review AI-generated HCC suggestions, compliance flags, and documentation outputs&nbsp; against source records, line by line. &nbsp; 

• Validate each diagnosis against MEAT criteria, diagnostic status (active vs. history), and&nbsp; current coding guidelines. &nbsp; 

• Build and maintain gold-standard chart sets used to test agent performance. • Score agent outputs for precision, recall, and false positive rate, and track trends across&nbsp; releases. &nbsp; 

• Identify error patterns and write clear, reproducible defect reports for engineering and&nbsp; data science. &nbsp; 

• Sign off on clinical quality before releases. &nbsp; 

Risk Adjustment Analysis&nbsp; 

• Apply CMS-HCC V28 logic, including hierarchies, interaction terms, and RAF&nbsp; calculation. &nbsp; 

• Assess RADV exposure on sampled charts: unsupported HCCs, error rates, and&nbsp; financial impact. &nbsp; 

• Track CMS model and rule changes and translate them into product requirements. &nbsp; 

Excel Modeling & Reporting&nbsp; 

• Build Excel models from scratch for RAF impact, PMPM and PMPY revenue, coding&nbsp; accuracy, and customer ROI. &nbsp; 

• Reconcile agent output data against claims, encounter, and chart review data. • Produce clear accuracy and impact reports for internal teams and customers. &nbsp; 

Cross-Functional Work&nbsp; 

• Turn clinical findings into specifications, acceptance criteria, and test cases for&nbsp; engineering. 

• Support customer teams with clinical answers on audits, accuracy questions, and coding&nbsp; disputes. &nbsp; 

Required Qualifications&nbsp; 

• Medical degree (MBBS, MD, or equivalent) or another clinical degree with deep risk&nbsp; adjustment experience. &nbsp; 

• 4 to 8 years in HCC risk adjustment, medical record review, coding audit, or clinical&nbsp; documentation integrity. &nbsp; 

• Strong command of CMS-HCC V28, MEAT, hierarchies, RAF calculation, and RADV&nbsp; standards. &nbsp; 

• Advanced Excel: pivot tables, XLOOKUP/INDEX-MATCH, nested formulas, and building&nbsp; calculation models from a blank sheet. &nbsp; 

• Hands-on experience reviewing charts and documenting coding errors with supporting&nbsp; evidence. &nbsp; 

• Precise, structured written communication. &nbsp; 

Preferred Qualifications&nbsp; 

• CRC, CPC, or CDIP certification. &nbsp; 

• Experience testing or validating AI, NLP, or other clinical software outputs. • Working knowledge of HEDIS measures or Medicaid risk models (CDPS). • SQL or Python for data pulls and analysis. &nbsp; 

• Experience at a health tech startup or risk adjustment vendor. &nbsp; 

Key Success Measures&nbsp; 

• Measurable improvement in agent precision and recall release over release. • Clinical errors caught before release, not by customers. &nbsp; 

• Accurate, reusable Excel models for RAF and ROI that the team relies on. • Defect reports engineering can act on without follow-up questions.

